1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:06,900
My story began in a small farming village in rural
Ethiopia.

2
00:00:07,100 --> 00:00:14,900
At just seven years old, I spent long days working
beside my mother in the fields.

3
00:00:15,100 --> 00:00:23,900
During school breaks, we pulled weeds and harvested
teff and wheat. The work was exhausting.

4
00:00:24,100 --> 00:00:31,900
Life was not easy, but I believed education could
change our future.

5
00:00:32,100 --> 00:00:41,900
When I ranked first in my school in the Grade 8
national exam, my mother sacrificed even more so I
could continue studying.

6
00:00:42,100 --> 00:00:49,900
At sixteen, I left my village to study. But during
school breaks, I always returned to our farm.

7
00:00:50,100 --> 00:00:57,900
At Addis Ababa University, I discovered computers,
programming and artificial intelligence.

8
00:00:58,100 --> 00:01:06,900
For the first time, I saw our fields differently.
Technology could distinguish weeds from crops.

9
00:01:07,100 --> 00:01:14,900
I imagined machines identifying weeds, helping harvest
crops and reducing farmers' exhausting labor.

10
00:01:15,100 --> 00:01:23,900
My journey began in the soil. My dream is to use
technology to make the next generation's journey
easier.
